                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "I can see this from the code - commit message is for the rationale.\n\nWould it make sense to default to the existing behavior to keep backward compatibility?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vishnunithyasoundhar S",
                        "email": "vishnunithyasoundhar.s@intel.com",
                        "username": "VishnuNithyaSoundharS"
                    },
                    "message": "Agreed. I have changed it so that it defaults to 0 on both mctp_eid and networkID when those arguments were not used, but still warn the user to make sure that they are informed."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
